  "description": "Speed made to endure Those who will take on any road, go any distance, and ride in any weather need a bike as strong and dependable as they are. With a high-performance carbon frame and telepathic handling, the RVR will satisfy the most discriminating endurance riders. There are no gimmicks, just efficiency, simplicity, and comfort. Ride as long as you wish. The RVR will never hold you back. Aerodynamic Design To make one of the most aerodynamic endurance bikes ever designed, the carbon frame was shaped through extensive CFD work and testing in the A2 wind tunnel by an engineering team that has developed record-breaking aero designs. Endurance Geometry Fine-tuned geometry puts riders in a more upright and relaxed position. This keeps you feeling fast and comfy during your longest rides and on imperfect road surfaces, letting you step on the gas harder and dig deeper late into every ride. Increased Comfort Suffer less during all-day adventures with a carbon frame lay-up engineered for increased vertical compliance that absorbs vibration and dampens impacts without sacrificing pedaling efficiency. Add extra squish with clearance for wider tires. Frame Material High Modulus Carbon Blend Frame Characteristic High Strength Frame Weight 1020 Grams (Size M) Max Tire 700 x 34+ Headset Spec 52mm Internal Front Spacing 100mm Rear Spacing 142mm Front Axle Specs M12 x 1.5 120-125mm Rear Axle Specs M12 x 1.0 164-167mm Seatpost Proprietary Aero Carbon Seatpost Binder Internal BB Standard T47 Max Chainring Size 54T Rotor Max Size (Front) 160mm Rotor Max Size (Rear) 160mm Front Derailleur Mount Braze-on Derailleur Hanger UDH Water Bottle Mounts Downtube, Seattube Cable Routing Internal Cable Routing",
